  {"comment": "SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT. A cubic lattice of 40 mm through the API (mitcad#1588): Plane1 (F1) through Z at 45 degrees from XZ; Sketch1 (F2) on it with the body diagonal c6 (the revolve's axis, from the far side of one corner ball to the far side of the other), the corner balls c7 and c8 (12 mm), the centre ball c9 (16 mm, not construction), the rod's side c12 1.6 mm off the diagonal from ball to ball, and a construction line c14 along a vertical edge of the cube; Revolve1 (F3) of every region beside c12 (the corner balls' halves, the rod's two pieces between the balls, its strip inside c9 and the cap of c9 beyond c12); Pipe1 (F4, 3.2 mm) along c14, joined; CircularPattern1 (F5) of both about X (3 over 180 degrees, symmetric) and about Z (4); Fillet1 (F6) of 1.6 mm at all 40 joints. The diagonal's copies land on one another three times over: elements 1, 2 and 3 are the other three diagonals, the rest left out; the pipe's 11 copies are the cube's other edges."},
